{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/818565-pugmire-monarchies-of-mau","id":818565,"title":"[Pugmire] Monarchies of Mau","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-28T10:38:42-08:00","id":818565,"title":"[Pugmire] Monarchies of Mau","content":"<b>Is there anything known about this land/game?</b> I'm much more cat person and base dedication to the dogs in <b>Pugmire</b> is the biggest problem to enjoy the whole idea of animal which inherited the world after humans.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Sidenote:</b> Yes, I'm a <b>Werewolf</b> ST also, but it's very different. Wolves are cool, dogs... Let just give me cat's suplement game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:43:57-08:00","id":818910,"title":"","content":"Cats aren't evil, but they do think of Man as having been subservient to their ancestors (as cats are wont to do), and possess an infinitely more individualistic and fractious culture (one character says they have seven words for betrayal...but this character is also noted to be a near-habitual borderline-liar, so it's probably more like &quot;seven words for doing things behind another's back, and only two of them count as a serious broach of trust&quot;). They're necromancers, but it's not because they have no respect for the dead, it's just that they see the dead and invisible as a quality of being, and figure out how to treat with them as a matter of opportunity.<br /> <br /> Much as how dogs hate badgers and their allies, cats have rodents-which is to say, the local variety of Skaven. The dominant faction in rat society is the Cult of the White Mice, who go closer to Man by invoking Their test subjects and acting as Man's proxies in Science. The sample cult trooper has an ability that inflicts debilitating pain on whoever he's attacking. Do the math.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T21:58:22-08:00","id":818989,"title":"","content":"Necromancers, &quot;pirates&quot; cats hunting Mices working Science! Oh hell yes!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y6OvsJqimfg\" data-code=\"Y6OvsJqimfg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Y6OvsJqimfg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-29-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T23:19:11-08:00","id":819019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/818565-pugmire-monarchies-of-mau?p=818910#post818910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much as how dogs hate badgers and their allies, cats have rodents-which is to say, the local variety of Skaven. The dominant faction in rat society is the Cult of the White Mice, who go closer to Man by invoking Their test subjects and acting as Man's proxies in Science. The sample cult trooper has an ability that inflicts debilitating pain on whoever he's attacking. Do the math.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you read &quot;all of civilization&quot; - me, I read it as not the Cult being the dominant faction in rat society, but as the Cult being pervasive throughout uplifted territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T09:56:31-08:00","id":819341,"title":"","content":"Wait...will there be options to eventually play rats and mice?<br /> Just asking for...reasons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:09:14-08:00","id":820406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/818565-pugmire-monarchies-of-mau?p=819341#post819341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait...will there be options to eventually play rats and mice?<br /> Just asking for...reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect not before cats and weasels.<br /> <br /> It should be easy enough to houserule, at least after felines/mustelides become availiable. Vanilla D&amp;D has smaller races and fans have codified rules for them soon enough. It should be easy to adapt.<br /> <br /> The speed really depends on how soon do NPC Rodents become availiable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T16:53:49-08:00","id":820643,"title":"","content":"Wait...I could also end up playing a Weasel?<br /> <br /> -Quietly Kickstarts-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T01:51:30-08:00","id":820838,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.....I wonder if there aren't still breeds of Cats that aren't complete a-holes. Maine Coon Cats, which appear to be descended from Norwegian Forest Cats IIRC, are certainly more &quot;dog-like&quot; in that they aren't generally as flaky as other cat breeds. Checking Wikipedia, the Manx and a few other breeds also qualify as &quot;dog-like&quot;, so hopefully there will be options down the road to play other domesticated animal types (Cats, Raccoons, Foxes, Mice/Rats).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1801-craftmason-bob-s-cousin","name":"Craftmason Bob's Cousin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T04:42:13-08:00","id":820880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craftmason Bob's Cousin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/818565-pugmire-monarchies-of-mau?p=820838#post820838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.....I wonder if there aren't still breeds of Cats that aren't complete a-holes. Maine Coon Cats, which appear to be descended from Norwegian Forest Cats IIRC, are certainly more &quot;dog-like&quot; in that they aren't generally as flaky as other cat breeds. Checking Wikipedia, the Manx and a few other breeds also qualify as &quot;dog-like&quot;, so hopefully there will be options down the road to play other domesticated animal types (Cats, Raccoons, Foxes, Mice/Rats).</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the more strongly domesticated breeds, like ragdolls, cornish rexes, maine coons, etc. are pretty sensible if you cater to their needs. I say this as an owner of a ragdoll for 3 years when I previously had experience owning tortoiseshell cats and siameses. The difference in personality is amazing.<br /> <br /> I'd be pretty surprised if those kinds of placid breeds weren't still around in the far future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T04:44:34-08:00","id":820883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craftmason Bob's Cousin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/818565-pugmire-monarchies-of-mau?p=820838#post820838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.....I wonder if there aren't still breeds of Cats that aren't complete a-holes. Maine Coon Cats, which appear to be descended from Norwegian Forest Cats IIRC, are certainly more &quot;dog-like&quot; in that they aren't generally as flaky as other cat breeds. Checking Wikipedia, the Manx and a few other breeds also qualify as &quot;dog-like&quot;, so hopefully there will be options down the road to play other domesticated animal types (Cats, Raccoons, Foxes, Mice/Rats).</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Eddy, Monarchies of Mau will be in the same world as Pugmire, and compatible with it, but it's not going to be a Pugmire supplement. It's going to be its own game. (Cats play differently from dogs, after all.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:27:23-08:00","id":821293,"title":"","content":"more like vampire the requiem to werewolf the forsaken. I'd definitely allow cross overs. Myself? I think playing a wolverine would be pretty rad. Imagine a wolverine with relic claws...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T23:44:50-08:00","id":821467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/818565-pugmire-monarchies-of-mau?p=820880#post820880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of the more strongly domesticated breeds, like ragdolls, cornish rexes, maine coons, etc. are pretty sensible if you cater to their needs. I say this as an owner of a ragdoll for 3 years when I previously had experience owning tortoiseshell cats and siameses. The difference in personality is amazing.<br /> <br /> I'd be pretty surprised if those kinds of placid breeds weren't still around in the far future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect its more a matter of culture and to a lesser extent biology of course Dogs think all cats are assholes.. they don't understand Cat culture at all. A cat would say &quot;A dog does not understand loyalty or love they give it to anyone and anything and never feel it as deeply as a cat.&quot; Dogs make friends easily and quickly, cats love fewer but more intensely. Dogs think cats believe humans served cats, cats know the truth it was a partnership because humans were bad at so many things(like hunting!) its was all a fair exchange and then they left and now we don't care because its not like we care about them.. baka humans..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T18:52:04-08:00","id":822038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/818565-pugmire-monarchies-of-mau?p=820643#post820643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait...I could also end up playing a Weasel?<br /> <br /> -Quietly Kickstarts-</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically the closest thing we are ever getting to a Redwall RPG... so yeah. I'm expecting we'll eventually see a lot of different types of animals become play